        <p class="eyebrow">About this episode</p>
        <h2>Removing the mask starts with an honest conversation.</h2>
        <div class="content-note"><strong>Content note</strong>This episode includes discussion of depression, anxiety, suicide loss, and personal mental-health struggles. Please listen with care and use the support resources available through Unmasked Culture or your local community if these topics affect you.</div>
        <p class="lede">In the inaugural episode of The Unmasked Podcast, hosts Mikel Stull and Zach introduce Unmasked Culture and the experiences that shaped its mission.</p>
        <p>Blending humor with honest reflection, they discuss depression, anxiety, grief, vulnerability, and the importance of finding safe people and helpful resources. They explain that “unmasked” is not a political statement; it is an invitation to remove the metaphorical masks that keep people isolated and pretending everything is fine.</p>
        <p>The conversation also introduces Unmasked Culture’s holistic approach to mental health, bringing physical, emotional, spiritual, and social well-being together. Mikel and Zach invite listeners to seek support and start honest conversations that remind others they are not alone.</p>

        <h3>In this episode</h3>
        <ul class="topic-list">
          <li>Why the word “unmasked” refers to authenticity rather than politics</li>
          <li>The four pillars of holistic mental health</li>
          <li>Mikel’s experience with depression, anxiety, and searching for support</li>
          <li>Zach’s experience of suffering quietly and why he now encourages conversation</li>
          <li>How personal loss helped shape the mission of Unmasked Culture</li>
          <li>Why vulnerability and healthy dialogue are central to the show</li>
          <li>How future episodes will balance humor, personal conversation, and education</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

